---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="Don't Be Broke — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Don't Be Broke</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Co-founder, non-profit</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        Don't Be Broke started as a pitch at Seattle Startup Weekend, built on the financial-literacy gap
        I'd identified through the MIT Inspire research: democratizing financial knowledge for teens who
        weren't getting it anywhere else. The concept won "Best Design" and "Audience Choice" at the
        event, which was enough momentum to turn it into an actual non-profit developing financial
        literacy materials.
      </p>
      <p class="blurb">
        It was my first time taking an idea all the way from a research question to something with a
        team, a pitch, and real output — a preview of the "own it end to end" pattern that shows up in
        everything I've done since.
      </p>
      <div class="stub-note">Have more specifics — team size, what materials you actually shipped, how long it ran? Send them over and I'll add them.</div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
